<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pata Pata</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">first recorded 1956 or 1959; best-known recording <a href="/years/1967">1967</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Pata Pata&quot; means &quot;touch touch&quot; in Xhosa, the language in which the song was first written and sung. It was also the name of a dance popular in the shebeens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannesburg">Johannesburg</a>'s townships in the mid-1950s, in which partners patted each other in time to the music. Makeba's song was not the only one the dance inspired.</p></div>
